.TH geectl-remote-set-project-meta 1  "geectl-remote-set-project-meta 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-set\-project\-meta \- Set a project\*(Aqs meta, field by field or whole from a file. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the write. Field flags change only the given fields; the rest of the meta is kept as it is. Clear a field with `\-\-from\-file`: fields the file omits are cleared
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote set\-project\-meta\fR [\fB\-\-from\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-scmsync\fR] [\fB\-\-devel\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-add\-person\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\-person\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set a project\*(Aqs meta, field by field or whole from a file. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the write. Field flags change only the given fields; the rest of the meta is kept as it is. Clear a field with `\-\-from\-file`: fields the file omits are cleared.
.PP
`\-\-from\-file FILE` writes the given meta file as the whole meta instead: the file\*(Aqs title, description, URL, scmsync, devel project, persons, groups, and repositories replace what the server holds, and fields the file omits are cleared. The file\*(Aqs project name must match the project. Settings outside the typed meta (locks, publish and build flags) survive, as in the field\-wise write. `\-\-from\-file` conflicts with every field and person flag.
.PP
`\-\-add\-person LOGIN:ROLE` grants a role to a person; `\-\-remove\-person LOGIN` removes every role that login holds. Removal applies before addition, so the pair moves a person to a new role — except a maintainer grant to someone who is not being removed, which applies first so a handover in one call keeps a maintainer. Roles: maintainer, bugowner, reviewer, reader, downloader.
.PP
The field\-wise write is not atomic: the field write runs first, then each person change is a separate read\-modify\-write, so a failure part\-way leaves the earlier changes applied, with no rollback. The `\-\-from\-file` write is a single `set_project_meta` call instead — one read\-modify\-write, one GET and at most one PUT when live — so a failure leaves either the old meta or the file\*(Aqs meta, never a half\-written mix. Dry\-run does not read the live meta, so a removal is not validated there: a login holding no role, and the last\-maintainer refusal, only fail with `\-\-live`. A dry run performs no fetch and cannot tell a changed repository from a pre\-existing one, so it validates no repositories, while `\-\-live` validates only the repositories it changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-file\fR \fI<FROM_FILE>\fR
Write the given meta file as the whole meta instead of setting fields: the file is a `<project>` document whose name matches the project. Conflicts with every field and person flag
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
The new title
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
The new description
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
The new URL
.TP
\fB\-\-scmsync\fR \fI<SCMSYNC>\fR
The new scmsync URL
.TP
\fB\-\-devel\-project\fR \fI<DEVEL_PROJECT>\fR
The new devel project
.TP
\fB\-\-add\-person\fR \fI<ADD_PERSON>\fR
Grant a role to a person: `LOGIN:ROLE`, repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\-person\fR \fI<REMOVE_PERSON>\fR
Remove a person: every role the login holds, repeatable
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project whose meta is written
